11. Prevent browser zoom during gameplay

Alva is a web game and repeated rapid taps must not cause the browser to zoom the webpage.

The repo already has several protections:

* .screen--battle { touch-action: none; }
* .battle-canvas { touch-action: none; }
* .screen--practice { touch-action: none; }
* .tc-btn { touch-action: none; }
* .tc-dpad { touch-action: none; }
* the document is already non-scrolling.

Do not delete or weaken those.

However, the current viewport is:

<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover">

Strengthen the game viewport so browser pinch/double-tap zoom does not activate during play.

Use:

<meta
  name="viewport"
  content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, maximum-scale=1, user-scalable=no, viewport-fit=cover"
>

Keep viewport-fit=cover.

Do not implement a JavaScript timer that tries to detect double taps.

Do not globally preventDefault() every touchstart/touchend event.

Do not add old Touch Events code beside the existing Pointer Events system.

The existing Pointer Events architecture should remain the source of gameplay input.

Also preserve:

touch-action: none;

on the battle/practice gameplay surfaces and the actual touch controls.

The end result must prevent rapid attack tapping from enlarging or shrinking the browser page.

